  "id": "group-role",
  "term": "group role",
  "definition": "A group role is the part a person takes within a group, such as leader, follower, naysayer, or observer. In this account, people may shift between roles, and those shifts can change both their own learning activity and the group’s overall way of engaging and learning together.",
